\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 TITCH V2.0 
\par The Drawing & Mind Mapping Application for the Psion 3a.
\par written by Martin R Sturgess
\par E-Mail: 100545.2662@compuserve.com
\par February 1996
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par {\i Use the diamond key to view this document in outline view.
\par }
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Introduction
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par TITCH is a vector based drawing/mind mapping application for the Psion 3a which gives  disk space savings of around 2000% compared with the more usual bitmap (.PIC ) based applications. 
\par 
\par TITCH Version 1 was marketed as primarily a drawing application. The emphasis on TITCH Version2 is it's use as a {\b mind mapping} application.
\par 
\par  Using TITCH you can create a graphical interface to your ideas or information. Text can be added horizontally or vertically and buttons placed which will automatically open then search any file created using the built in applications. 
\par 
\par For more information about Mind Mapping look for books by Tony Buzan. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Disclaimer
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par 
\par I do not accept any responsibility or liability for any damage to hardware or data caused by the use of TITCH. 
\par 
\par  I will, however, do my best to assist in the event of problems. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Installing
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab Back up your data.
\par 
\par 2.\tab Copy TITCHV2.OPA to M:\\APP\\ ( or B:\\APP\\ or A:\\APP\\) and install it from the System Screen.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Create a sub-directory \\APP\\TITCH\\ and copy UP08.FON, DOWN08.FON and TITCH.HLP to it. TITCH.HLP can be removed if you do not require online help. The two font files can be removed if you do not require vertical text.
\par 
\par 4.\tab Familiarize yourself with the contents of this manual! 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par {\ul Note for version 1 users
\par }Delete TITCH.HLP from \\OPD\\ and TITCHV1.opa from \\APP\\
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Changes from Version 1
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab 
You can now insert hyperlinks which will launch a file using the built in psion applications. Valid file types are Agenda, Data, Sheet, Word, Text, OPL and OPO. These links can also contain search text.
\par 
\par 2.\tab The need to use two modes (Draw and Update) has been removed. 
\par \tab 
\par \tab {\i To }{\b\i launch}{\i  linked files you now toggle between hyperlinks using the }{\b\i <Space>}{\i  key  or position cursor over the link and press <Enter>. 
\par \tab 
\par \tab To }{\b\i edit}{\i  objects  toggle between them using  }{\b\i <Tab>}{\i .
\par }
\par 3.\tab Lines can now be moved !!
\par 
\par 4.\tab The diamond key now launches an edit filter dialogue which removes the need to toggle through all types of object when,  for instance, you wish to only move boxes.
\par 
\par 5.\tab When using <Space> or <Tab> to move between objects the <Shift> modifier key reverses the direction. 
\par 
\par 6.\tab Text and Links can now be edited. 
\par 
\par 7.\tab Swiss text style added.
\par 
\par 8.\tab 8 point Vertical text ( up and down) added.
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 The Main Features of  TITCH
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Save Time and Disk Space
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par 480x160 ( full screen size) black & grey TITCH drawings are typically less than 1K in size compared to the 19K or so required for PIC based drawing applications. 
\par 
\par {\b\i This now makes the storage of large numbers of drawing files possible for the average Psion user.
\par }
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Editable Drawings
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Since TITCH files are {\b vector} based, objects and text can be moved or deleted at any time.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 HyperLinks
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par TITCH utilises a powerful {\b\i hyperlinking }system allowing drawings to be linked to other drawings OR files created using th
e built in Psion Applications. You can even launch .OPO files ( but not applications). Some file types allow the use of search strings in the link.
\par 
\par  Any part of a TITCH drawing can be {\b\i exported }to PIC format to give compatability with other drawing applications.
\par 
\par TITCH drawings can also contain {\b\i links} to PIC files. This powerful facility allows you to  create a library of small PIC files, any of which can then be displayed within a TITCH drawing. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Templates
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par TITCH incorporates a{\b  }{\b\i template  }facility allowing each drawing to display any other drawing in the background. This will be useful if you regularly wish to incorporate a standard logo or table in your drawing. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Drawing Grid
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par TITCH can display a black or grey drawing {\b\i grid }of any size which will assist you when aligning objects or drawing to scale. 
\par 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 What TITCH can Draw
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 *\tab Lines (thick and thin)  
\par *\tab Circles (filled and unfilled)
\par *\tab Boxes (filled, unfilled and patterned)
\par *\tab Text (including vertical text !)
\par *\tab Triangles,Diamonds,Pentagons,Hexagons,Heptagons and Octagons ( unfilled)
\par *\tab The contents of any PIC File
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Remember that you can create your own objects by first drawing them using the built in objects then exporting to a PIC File. 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Moving between Drawings
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par In addition to the standard Psion way of opening files from the File menu or the System Screen, T ITCH drawings can also be opened using  Link Buttons that you insert into your drawing.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 File Menu - Go to Home Page 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par This will open the drawing last opened from the System screen or the last file opened using the {\b Open} option from the {\b File} menu
\par 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Moving the Cursor
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Use the arrow keys to  move the cursor 10 pixels at a time. 
\par To move 1 pixel at a time hold down the PSION key while using the arrow keys.
\par 
\par To jump to a specific position use the {\b Screen} menu and select{\b  Jump To}. Note that immediately after drawing a line the jump position will be the {\b start of the Line}. 
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Using the Drawing Grid
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1.\tab From the {\b Draw }Menu select {\b Display Grid
\par 
\par }2.\tab Select the Grid size and colour from the resulting dialogue.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 Note that the  Grid is {\i not} written to the TITCH drawing. To remove the Grid select {\b Refresh }from the {\b Screen }Menu.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 How to Draw Objects
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab First move the cursor to the start position for the object then select the object to be drawn from the {\b Draw} menu.
\par 
\par 2.\tab Select the object characteristics from the resulting dialogue box.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Use the arrow keys to move to the end point of the object. 
\par 
\par \tab For Lines this will be other end of the line.
\par \tab For Boxes this will be the opposite corner of the box.
\par \tab For Circles and polygons this will set the radius of the object - the original cursor position is the centre of the polygon or circle.
\par 
\par 4.\tab Press <Enter> 
\par 
\par 5.\tab Large objects will be drawn immediately. For small objects (not Lines)  you will be prompted with {\b Move<Enter><Esc>}. 
\par 
\par 6.\tab Use the arrow keys to move the object to it's final position then press <Enter>. You can press <Esc> at any time to cancel the object.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Inserting Links
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Use the LINK facility to create large virtual drawings which consist of individual drawings linked together via link buttons. You can also link to other types of file.
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1.\tab Select {\b Link} from the {\b Insert }Menu.
\par 
\par 2.\tab Select a file name and type from the resulting dialogues.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Enter search text if you want to jump to a specific part of the file. you can for example jump to a specific record in your address book ( created with the DATA app) by entering some unique text contained in that record.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Move the Link button to a suitable position in your drawing and press <Enter>.
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Using Links
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab Press the <Space> key. You may need type press <Esc> first.
\par 
\par \tab The first Link button will be highlighted by a flashing cursor. 
\par 
\par 2.\tab To open the Linked file press <Enter> or, to move to another Link press the <Space> key again.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 Use the <Shift> and <Space> keys together to reverse the direction in which you move through the objects.
\par 
\par 
\par Press <Esc> to cancel if moving between Link buttons using the <Space> key.
\par 
\par {\i Note that you can also open Links by positioning the cursor over the Links and pressing <Enter>.
\par 
\par }When opening a file from one of the built in applications quitting the application should take you back to TITCH. if you wish to keep the application open use <Shift><System>  to cycle back to TITCH.
\par 
\par Note that some file types allow the use of search strings which will allow you to automatically  jump to a specific point in the file.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Note for JBData Users
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Any dbf files opened by TITCH will use the buily in DATA application. 
Opening the file in JBData whilst DATA has it open will generate an error. You are advised to install the DATA or RunImg applications so that you have a visible indication that DATA has a file open.
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Templates
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Any TITCH drawing can be used as a template for any other TITCH drawing. This powerful facility obviates the need to draw the same series of objects in multiple drawings thus saving disk space. Templates can be added or removed at any time.
\par 
\par Note that Templates always appear in the background to a drawing, i.e. all objects are drawn {\i over} the template. Templates are {\i not} recursive, i.e. any links or templates contained {\i within} a template will not be displayed.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 To add a Link to a Template
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1.\tab From the {\b Edit} menu select {\b Template.
\par }
\par 2.\tab Select "Add Link to Template" from the dialogue box.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Select a TITCH drawing from the resulting dialogue box.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 To remove a Link to a Template
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1. From the {\b Edit }menu select {\b Template
\par }
\par 2. Select "Remove link to Existing Template".
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 PIC Files
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Any part of a TITCH drawing can be exported to a PIC file. This gives compatibility with existing drawing applications for the Psion3a.
\par 
\par TITCH drawings can also display PIC Files. When a PIC File is inserted into a TITCH drawing it is actually only a LINK to the PIC file which is inserted. This approach saves disk space since one PIC file can be displayed in multiple drawings.
\par 
\par If for example you wish to use TITCH to draw electronic circuit diagrams it would prove time consuming to redraw each component. Instead, draw the component once then 
export the component to a PIC file. The component can then be inserted into any TITCH drawing! One caveat is that TITCH cannot (at present) rotate PIC Files so you will need to have a separate PIC File for each orientation of the component.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Exporting to a PIC File
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab Place the cursor at the top left of the area to be exported.
\par 
\par 2.\tab From the {\b Extract }menu select {\b Extract to Pic.
\par }
\par 3.\tab Choose if you wish to include the grey plane from the resulting dialogue.
\par 
\par 4.\tab Select area with the arrow keys then press <Enter>.
\par 
\par 5.\tab Supply the file name in the resulting dialogue.
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Importing a Link file
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1.\tab Move the cursor to the top left of where the Pic file is to appear.
\par 
\par 2.\tab from the {\b Insert }Menu select {\b Pic File}.
\par 
\par 3.\tab Select a PIC file from the resulting dialogue.
\par 
\par 4.\tab If the PIC File is small you will be prompted with {\i Move<Enter><Esc>}. Move the PIC file to it's final position and press <Enter>. 
\par \tab Large PIC Files will be placed immediately without the ability to adjust the final position.
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Updating Drawings
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 1.\tab Use the diamond key to select which objects you wish to enter.
\par 
\par 2.\tab Use the tab key to move between objects. Use the Menu to move objects or to edit text and links.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
Note that large object information will be prefixed with "*" which will indicate that the object will not be highlighted and is too large to move. Large objects {\i can} be deleted.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Deleting Objects
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 
\par 1.\tab Use the <Tab> key to step through the objects in reverse chronological order i.e. the last object drawn will be the first object selected. use <Shift><Tab> to move through the file in the opposite direction.
\par 
\par 2.\tab To delete the object press <Delete> or from the {\b Edit} menu select {\b Delete Object
\par }
\par 4.\tab Press <Enter> to confirm deletion or <Esc> to cancel
\par 
\par 5.\tab Press <Enter> to redraw the screen or <Tab> to move to the next object without redrawing.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Moving Objects
\par \pard\plain \s15\qj\fi-360\li720\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720 \f42 
\par 1.\tab Use DIAMOND key to set the edit selection filter.
\par 
\par 2.\tab Use the <Tab> ( or <Shift><Tab>) key to step through the objects.
\par 
\par 3.\tab From the {\b Move} Menu select {\b Move Object.} 
\par 
\par 4.\tab Use the Arrow keys to move the Object then press <Enter>. 
\par \tab <Esc> will cancel the move.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 Where the TITCH Files are stored
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 DRG Files
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par TITCH drawings have the extension ".DRG" and are stored in the \\TITCH\\ directory at the top level of any disk on which you create drawings. The \\TITCH\\ directory is created automatically.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 PIC Files
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par PIC files have the extension ".PIC" and are stored in the \\TITCH\\PIC\\ directory. The \\PIC directory is created automatically.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Curs.pic and Titch.reg
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par These are files internal to TITCH and are stored in the M:\\OPD\\ directory
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 Temporary Files
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par Temp.pic is created in the M:\\OPD\\ directory whilst moving objects on screen. This is usually removed immediately after use but may remain if TITCH exits abnormally. 
\par 
\par It will be removed the next time you launch TITCH.
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sa120\sl240\slmult0\keepn \b\f42 LINKED Files
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par If you insert Links to other drawings or PIC files TITCH will search for them using the following algorithms.
\par 
\par {\ul Drawings and Templates
\par }
\par TITCH first searches for the drawing with the same name and in the same directory and disk as when the link was created. 
\par 
\par If not found TITCH then searches on disk M: in the same directory  then M:\\TITCH\\ then M:\\TITCH\\LIB\\. This search is then repeated for disks A: and B:.
\par 
\par {\ul PIC Files
\par }
\par TITCH first searches for the PIC file with the same name and in the same directory and disk as when the link was created. 
\par 
\par If not found TITCH then searches on disk M: in the same directory  then M:\\TITCH\\ then M:\\TITCH\\PIC\\. This search is then repeated for disks A: and B:.
\par 
\par 
\par If a drawing or PIC File is not found an error will be displayed and written to the log screen which can be viewed using the {\b Log} menu.
\par 
\par If TITCH cannot find PIC files when the drawing is opened you will be prompted to delete the links from the drawing. The Log screen will give details of what files could not be found.
\par 
\par {\ul Built in Applications
\par }
\par TITCH will search for the file with the same name and in the same directory as when the file was created. it will then search the normal directory on M: , A: and B:
\par 
\par If not found TITCH then searches  M:\\TITCH\\ then M:\\TITCH\\LIB\\. This search is then repeated for disks A: and B:.
\par 
\par Normal directories are:
\par 
\par \\WRD\\ \tab Word and Text 
\par \\SPR\\ \tab Sheet
\par \\DAT\\\tab Data
\par \\OPO\\\tab OPO files created from OPL
\par \\OPL\\\tab OPL program files
\par \\AGN\\\tab Agenda
\par 
\par \pard\plain \s1\qc\sa240\sl480\slmult0\keepn \b\f42\fs48 A Note on the \\LIB\\ directory.
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa240\sl240\slmult0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760 \f42 
\par You may wish to create a large virtual drawing which actually consists of several drawings which are linked. Any drawings stored in \\TITCH\\LIB\\ will still be found if they are referenced by a LINK button but they will not appear on the System Screen. 

\par 
